{"name":"Jungle Cloak","hex":"#686959","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jungle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, lush, undeveloped, humid forest, especially in a tropical region, thick with vegetation and wildlife; a tropical  rainforest.","Any uncultivated tract of forest or scrub habitat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["(Of musical beat, rhythm, etc.) resembling the fast-paced drumming of traditional peoples of the jungle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle"},{"term":"cloak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long outer garment worn over the shoulders covering the back; a cape, often with a hood.","A blanket-like covering, often metaphorical."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover as with or like a cloak.","To cover up, hide or conceal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jungle","blocks":[{"text":"A jungle is an area of land covered with dense forest and tangled vegetation, usually in tropical climates. Application of the term has varied greatly during the past century. Because jungles occur on all inhabited landmasses and may incorporate numerous vegetation and land types in different climatic zones, the wildlife of jungles cannot be straightforwardly defined."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg/330px-%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle","wikidata":"Q191086"},{"title":"Cloak","blocks":[{"text":"A cloak is a type of loose garment worn over clothing, mostly but not always, as outerwear for outdoor wear, which serves the same purpose as an overcoat and protects the wearer from the weather. It may form part of a uniform. People in many different societies may wear cloaks. Over time, cloak designs have changed to match fashion and available textiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg/330px-Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloak","wikidata":"Q516992"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/500px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/1280px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/500px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jungle on Tioman Island, Malaysia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATioman_Rainforest.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg/500px-Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg/1280px-Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg/500px-Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"El Yunque National Forest in Puerto Rico, the only tropical rainforest managed by the U.S. National Forest Service","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Mosnticulo_de_los_anranjos.jpg/500px-Mosnticulo_de_l